# Trioloo ERP - frontend PRODUCTION build environment.
#
# Loaded automatically by `vite build` (mode = production). Committed deliberately:
# it contains no secret, and leaving it out is what made a production bundle call
# the operator's own machine.
#
# DEP-002.c - the frontend and the API SHARE ONE ORIGIN in production. The browser
# therefore makes SAME-ORIGIN requests and no CORS entry is required.
#
# The value is EMPTY ON PURPOSE. api.ts builds every request as `${API_BASE_URL}${path}`,
# so an empty base yields a relative `/api/...` URL that resolves against whatever origin
# served the page - https://user.trioloo.com in production.
#
# The empty string survives: api.ts uses `??`, which falls back only on null/undefined,
# never on ''. Deleting this line does NOT mean "no base URL" - it silently restores the
# development fallback `http://localhost:8080`, which in production is the operator's own
# computer and is blocked as mixed content. Do not remove it.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
